# Golden claim cases (obviously fictional). The oracle is written from the fixtures BY HAND, never
# read back from the pipeline: expected_recommendation, expected_indemnity_cents and expected_flags
# are the independently hand-computed answers, so a metric scored against them cannot be satisfied
# by the pipeline agreeing with itself. `planted` is the synthetic NRIC in that claim's file; the
# redact-before-model-and-write step must mask it, so pii_safety goes red if it survives.
